<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hwa Shin says selling own shares.</title>
<headline>Hwa Shin says selling own shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auto parts maker Hwa Shin Manufacturing Co Ltd said on Monday it would sell 43,140 shares of its own common stock to raise working capital.</p>
<p>After the sell-off, the South Korean company will not hold any of its own shares.  </p>
<p>The sales, representing 1.85 percent of Hwa Shin's share capital, will take place at any time between October 18, 1996, and January 17, 1997, a company statement said.</p>
<p>The statement said the shares would be sold on the open market at the previous day's closing price. Hyundai Securities will handle the sale.</p>
<p>Hwa Shin's shares closed down 300 won at 19,600 on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
